    <!-- A section that grows in height: a till receipt on an 80mm roll, from a starting size of 80mm by 40mm. The
         flow is one page as tall as the content and the margin, and the printer cuts the paper where it ends.
         Expected, top to bottom, on one page 80mm wide and far taller than 40mm:
           1  The shop's name and address, centred
           2  Thirty lines of the order: the quantity, the item, which wraps when it is long, and the amount on the
              right
           3  The subtotal, the tax and the total
           4  The card slip, which asks for a page break before it and starts none: it follows the total
           5  The footer, pinned to the bottom, right under the slip, not at the foot of the starting size
    -->
